A 2021 arXiv research paper by Shaul Zemel. Introduction

Real Clifford algebras were defined, in some small dimensions, in the second half of the 19th century, in attempts to create a formalism for movements in space. With time they played a larger and larger role in the understanding of quadratic vector spaces, though many of the explicit results were given over the real or complex number fields (see, e.g.,
